---
description: House rules for the Costa Mesa Jiu Jitsu website. Applies to every change.
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` in the repo root before changing anything, and follow it exactly. The short version:

1. Work on the `staging` branch. Never commit to, push to, or open a pull request you intend to merge yourself into `main`. Pull requests from your work use `staging` as the base branch.
2. Edit the existing code. Do not add frameworks, build tools, packages, new stylesheets or new script files. Do not rewrite or restructure the site.
3. Never hand-edit generated files (`free-trial/`, `kids-jiu-jitsu/`, `pricing/`, `private-lessons/`, `brady-fink/`, `upcoming-tournaments/`, `privacy-policy/`, `terms-of-service/`, `waiver/`, `assets/site.css`, `assets/pages.js`, `_redirects`, `sitemap.xml`, `robots.txt`, `404.html`, top-level `llms.txt`). Edit `index.html` or the files in `tools/`, then rebuild.
4. Keep changes small. Do not reformat or clean up code you were not asked to change.
5. Run `python3 tools/check.py` before every push and fix everything it reports.
6. Do not touch the text message consent checkbox, the privacy or SMS terms wording, form handling, tracking scripts, `netlify.toml`, `.github/` or `_redirects` without Mitchell's say-so.
7. Never use em dashes in site copy. The address is always "2428 Newport Blvd, Unit 7".
8. Only Mitchell approves and merges into `main`. When the work is ready, open a pull request from `staging` into `main` with a plain-English summary and stop there.
